    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "What it works out",
      "items": [
        "z = re + i*im",
        "(a + i*b) * (c + i*d) = (a*c - b*d) + i*(a*d + b*c)",
        "|z| = sqrt(re*re + im*im), and the angle is atan2(im, re)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why a structure and not complex.h",
      "items": [
        "Many small compilers do not give <complex.h> or float _Complex",
        "<complex.h> gives the macro complex, thus no module here could carry that name",
        "A structure of two members works on every compiler"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "What it costs you",
      "items": [
        "One complex multiplication is four real ones and two additions",
        "That cost carries into every module built on it",
        "It holds its values in the same width as the rest of the library"
